K90 builtin: crown already-installed manager at first zygote

SukiSU-Ultra manager 42d7fda / 40900 only looks for an injected
[ksu_driver] fd. It never calls reboot(0xDEADBEEF, 0xCAFEBABE) itself.
The kernel injects that fd on zygote setresuid only after throne_tracker
has matched the APK signature. Upstream only searches /data/app when
packages.list changes, and boot-completed is prune-only (and needs
ksud). After fastboot boot the manager is already installed, so it is
never crowned and the official APK shows 未安装.

Call track_throne(false) from on_post_fs_data (first zygote, /data
ready). Skip once builtin searches at this point.

--- a/kernel/runtime/ksud.c
+++ b/kernel/runtime/ksud.c
@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@
 
     ksu_load_allow_list();
     ksu_observer_init();
+    /* Official manager never probes reboot(); it needs a crowned UID so
+     * zygote setresuid can inject [ksu_driver]. Search /data/app now.
+     */
+    track_throne(false);
     // sanity check, this may influence the performance
     stop_input_hook();
     ksu_selinux_hide_handle_post_fs_data();
